                <p class="mb-0">
                    HTML form basics start with the <code>&lt;form&gt;</code>
                    element and controls such as <code>&lt;input&gt;</code>,
                    <code>&lt;textarea&gt;</code>, <code>&lt;select&gt;</code>,
                    <code>&lt;option&gt;</code>, and <code>&lt;button&gt;</code>.
                    Labels should be associated with controls using matching
                    <code>for</code> and <code>id</code> values. Attributes such
                    as <code>name</code>, <code>value</code>, <code>placeholder</code>,
                    <code>required</code>, <code>readonly</code>, and
                    <code>disabled</code> provide additional control over
                    form behavior.
